+// before any state/data/event commit and never publish an effect; the strip
+// is sticky-gated, so a refused launch commits no graphics) is recovered by
+// replaying the refused program body on CPU, exactly once per session, from
+// the owner's retained PRE-LAUNCH snapshot (the device-side bank copy recorded
+// ahead of the refused dispatch). Everything captured here is what the
+// protocol requires for the rejection evidence: the image identity, the
+// entry/continuation PC, the input-state digest, the literal-effect metadata
+// and the decoded rejection reason. Any refusal that does not meet the
+// recovery preconditions is a strict fatal stop (report and stop cleanly).
