+    // the prior work and the reset instead of retiring first and then shipping a
+    // control-only batch that the next barrier must retire again.
+    //
+    // Ordering: every admitted launch is flushed into its own submitted batch at
+    // launch time, so the pending batch holds only later uploads/controls; the
+    // zeroes execute after every earlier launch in GPU stream order, and earlier
+    // launches keep their own controls. LiteralCommands only describes FUTURE
+    // launches; the verifier replay restores each launch's retained snapshot.
+    //
+    // CPU mirror: ps2_memory.cpp (VIF1_FBRST bit0) calls this BEFORE it memsets
+    // vif1_regs. That order is required: the barrier may replay refused launches
+    // on CPU, which restores their launch-time controls into vif1_regs; the
+    // memset afterwards leaves the mirror zeroed for CPU fallback and reads.
+    //
+    // Capacity: the old order drained first and appended to an empty batch. A
+    // nearly full pending batch must be submitted (ordered, no wait) rather than
+    // overflow, which throws on GPU-owned sessions and rotates away history in
+    // record-only mode.
